# Project and toolchain naming and terminology

  (Links to all of these projects can be found in the oneMath repository on
  GitHub.)

  - oneAPI: An open, free, and standards-based programming system that
    provides portability and performance across accelerators and generations
    of hardware. oneMath is just one of its components (the others being
    oneDPL, oneDNN, oneCCL, oneDAL, and oneTBB).

  - oneMath: An open-source implementation of the oneAPI/oneMath
    specification. It is this build2 project's upstream.

  - oneMKL (Intel oneMKL): One of the backends supported by oneMath; primarily
    used for Intel CPUs and GPUs.

  - oneAPI DPC++/C++ compiler: The open source (Intel) project upon which the
    Intel oneAPI DPC++/C++ (SYCL) compiler is based. It is based on clang but
    is quite different in many respects. Referred to as "Open DPC++" by
    oneMath.

  - Intel oneAPI DPC++/C++ compiler (icpx): Intel's proprietary SYCL
    compiler. Based on the oneAPI DPC++/C++ compiler mentioned above. This is
    the only compiler this build2 project has been tested with. Referred to as
    "Intel DPC++" by oneMath.

# Setting up oneMKL and the Intel oneAPI DPC++/C++ compiler (icpx)

  - Installation: On Linux, set up the apt repository as per the Intel oneMKL
    website. Then install the intel-oneapi-mkl-devel-2025.2 and
    intel-oneapi-compiler-dpcpp-cpp-2025.2 packages. Those should be the only
    ones required.

  - Run the oneMKL `setvars.sh` script (sets various environment variables).

  - Add the icpx compiler tools to the PATH:

    export PATH=/opt/intel/oneapi/compiler/2025.2/bin/compiler/:$PATH

    This is for clang-offload-packager (see sycl_compilation.build).

  Verify everything worked by running `icpx --help`.

# Upstream build: configuring

   cmake -DREF_BLAS_ROOT=<refblas_root> \
         -DREF_LAPACK_ROOT=<refblas_root> \
         -DBUILD_EXAMPLES=off \
         -DBUILD_FUNCTIONAL_TESTS=on \
         -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=debug \
         -DCMAKE_VERBOSE_MAKEFILE=on -DCMAKE_COLOR_MAKEFILE=off \
         <oneMath-src-dir>

  Where <refblas_root> is the parent directory of `include` and `lib`
  directories containing the reference BLAS and LAPACK libraries used to
  verify the oneMath tests' own answers. I would recommend installing the
  reference BLAS/LAPACK mentioned in
  https://uxlfoundation.github.io/oneMath/building_and_running_tests.html.

# Creating a build2 configuration

  bdep init -C @cfg cc -- \
    config.cxx='/opt/intel/oneapi/compiler/2025.2/bin/icpx' \
    config.cxx.id=clang \
    config.c='/opt/intel/oneapi/compiler/2025.2/bin/icx' \
    config.c.id=clang \
    config.liboneMath_tests.reference_blas_incdir=<refblas_root>/include \
    config.liboneMath_tests.reference_blas_libdir=<refblas_root>/lib \
    config.liboneMath.enable_mklcpu_backend=true

  See the Upstream build section above RE the reference BLAS/LAPACK root
  directory.

