# Upstream tests

## test_main_blas_{ct,rt}

I get 3 failures in test_main_blas_{ct,rt}. But if I run each of them
individually, they succeed. This suggests a problem in the upstream test code.

## test_main_sparse_blas{ct,rt}

These fail undeterministically (segfaults, invalid pointers, or just lots of
test failures until one of the former occurs). But the same goes for these
tests in the upstream build. So again, seems like a problem in the upstream
code.

## test_main_rng_{ct,rt}

They visibly run at a different pace than the upstream tests. The biggest and
most apparent problem is that the following two tests are much slower
downstream (30s vs. 200ms):

Philox4x32x10UniformStdDeviceMomentsTestsSuite/Philox4x32x10UniformStdDeviceMomentsTests.RealSinglePrecision/Intel_R__Core_TM__Ultra_7_265K
Philox4x32x10UniformStdDeviceMomentsTestsSuite/Philox4x32x10UniformStdDeviceMomentsTests.RealDoublePrecision/Intel_R__Core_TM__Ultra_7_265K

But then some of our tests run much faster (0ms vs. non-zero (10, 20...)  ms
upstream.

Obviously seems like something serious is wrong. Did not have time to get to
the bottom of it but it seems like differences in SYCL scheduling/offloading
and/or concurrency.

Oddly, adding -g makes our tests much faster, but still slower than
upstream. I did also try the same flags they use for release builds (-O3
-DNDEBUG).

Some LLMs said -fsycl-device-code-split=per_kernel which upstream uses might
be the key difference but it makes the link take much longer and made tests
run much slower but I don't think I ever tried this flag on the RNG tests so
this needs to be tried, if only on the RNG tests.

Our compilation and link flags and the linked libraries are pretty much
identical to upstream (and I tried all variations of -O2 and -O3 with
-DNDEBUG) except for the things in sycl_compilation.build, so the latter
probably the first thing to look into. See the comments in that file for
details.

Disabling MKLGPU in the upstream build did not make their tests slower so the
problem is not that we don't have GPU support enabled downstream yet.
